      "id": "Q1~0",
      "text": "A legally protectable settled possessor facing attempted interference with the identified property has an independent possessory basis for an injunction restraining that interference, without first establishing proprietary title.",
      "submitted_text": "E1 has an independently supportable possessory ground for injunctive restraint against E2's interference with settled possession of E3, notwithstanding E1's failure to establish proprietary title. This conclusion depends on S3, which depends on S2's accepted judicial settled-possession classification and S1's preservation of possession despite title non-proof. It supports protection against interference without determining every independent requirement for injunctive relief or confirming ownership.",
