    {
      "id": "Q3~3",
      "text": "An injunction justified on an independent possessory ground does not, by virtue of that ground or relief alone, constitute confirmation of proprietary title for the possessor or rejection of another party's possible ownership.",
      "submitted_text": "The injunction ground protecting E1's possession of E3 against E2's interference does not, by itself, confirm E1's ownership or determine E2's competing proprietary claim. S5 depends on the possessory basis established through S3. Its conclusion is a non-entailment concerning proprietary title, not an affirmative finding that either litigant lacks ownership.",
